# Copy this file to `.env` (same folder), then replace [ADD KEY HERE] below
# with your OpenAI key. Keep the line with no spaces around the `=`:
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-abc123...
#
# Get a key from https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#
# `.env` is gitignored, so your real key is never committed.
#
# Leave this unset and the app simply skips the voice step; everything else
# works as normal.
#
# SECURITY: EXPO_PUBLIC_ values are inlined into the JS bundle in plain text
# and can be extracted from any build of the app. Fine for a personal build on
# your own phone. Before TestFlight or the App Store this call has to move
# behind a server that holds the key.

EXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_API_KEY=[ADD KEY HERE]

# Optional. Leave both unset unless you want to pin one specific model.
#
# By default the app tries several models in order and uses the first one your
# OpenAI project is allowed to use, so a restricted model allow-list does not
# break anything. Setting either of these disables that and pins your choice —
# if the pinned model is not permitted, the call simply fails.
#
#   Transcription: gpt-4o-mini-transcribe, whisper-1, gpt-4o-transcribe, gpt-transcribe
#   Text/vision:   gpt-4o-mini, gpt-4.1-mini, gpt-4o
# EXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_TEXT_MODEL=
